<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.4 </span>Caption-Level Hallucination: CHAIR Results</h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S5.T5" title="In 5.4 Caption-Level Hallucination: CHAIR Results ‣ 5 Results ‣ Beyond Dominant Patches: Spatial Credit Redistribution For Grounded Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the CHAIR metrics for the six models on 3,000 COCO val2014 captions. POPE gains (Type II) transfer to open-ended caption hallucinations (Type I).</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>CHAIR metrics on COCO captions (3,000 images), comparing vanilla baseline against SCR. CHAIR evaluates open-ended caption generation (Type I). Average reductions: CHAIR-s <math id="S5.T5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>45</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45\%</annotation></semantics></math>, CHAIR-i <math id="S5.T5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="48\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>48</mn><mo mathsize="1.110em">%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">48\%</annotation></semantics></math> relative. Full multi-baseline comparisons (OPERA, VCD, VLI, CRoPS, SID) are in Appendix B.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T5.7" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:345.0pt;height:84.7pt;vertical-align:-40.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-26.2pt,6.4pt) scale(0.868283099848455,0.868283099848455) ;">
