</section>
<section id="S5.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">5.5 </span>Theoretical Prediction Validation</h3>

<div id="S5.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">With SCR, we validate four empirical predictions across all six models utilizing the POPE-Adversarial split. These predictions are labeled <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P1</span>-<span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4</span> and are distinct from the three formal Propositions in Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Methodology ‣ Beyond Dominant Patches: Spatial Credit Redistribution For Grounded Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>: <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P1</span> and <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P2</span> are observational predictions derived from the hallucination-entropy relationship (Section <a href="#S3" title="3 Methodology ‣ Beyond Dominant Patches: Spatial Credit Redistribution For Grounded Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>); <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P3</span> is the empirical test of Proposition 2 (spatial autocorrelation); <span id="S5.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P4</span> is the empirical test of Proposition 3 (inverted-U <math id="S5.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> relationship). Proposition 1 (norm-credit proxy) is validated separately in Appendix C.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS5.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS5.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS5.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">P1: Entropy-Hallucination Correlation.</span> Across samples and models, lower spatial credit entropy is associated with higher hallucination rates. <a href="#S5.T6" title="In 5.5 Theoretical Prediction Validation ‣ 5 Results ‣ Beyond Dominant Patches: Spatial Credit Redistribution For Grounded Vision-Language Models" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> shows negative correlations across architectures.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T6" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="font-size:90%;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 6: </span>Entropy-hallucination correlation (Pearson <math id="S5.T6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>) across models.</figcaption>
